<p><strong>Exercise:</strong>Make an ordered list ( using the ol and li tags ). For each item, output a math problem using each operator least once and two numbers between 1 and 9 ( i.e. 1+9=????? ).</p>

<ol>

    <li>
        6 + 6 = 
        <bx:output >
            #6+6#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        10 - 9 = 
        <bx:output >
            #9-8#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        8 x 8 = 
        <bx:output >
            #8*8#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        9 / 3 = 
        <bx:output >
            #9/3#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        5^2 = 
        <bx:output >
            #5^2#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        Remainder of 11 / 2 = 
        <bx:output >
            #7%2#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        9 / 2 to the nearest integer = 
        <bx:output >
            #9\2#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        Range from 1-5 = (Code is #1..5# but trying to parse it as a string produces an error)
    </li>
    <li>
        Range from 1-5 excluding start value = (Code is #1>..5#)
    </li>
    <li>
        Range from 1-5 excluding end value = (Code is #1..<5#)
    </li>
    <li>
        Range from 1-5 excluding start and end values = (Code is #1>..<5#)
    </li>
    <li>
        6 + 1 (by increment) = 
        <bx:output>
            #++6#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        2 - 1 (by decrement) = 
        <bx:output >
            #--2#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        8 negated = 
        <bx:output >
            #-8#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        4 positive = 
        <bx:output >
            #+4#
        </bx:output>
    </li>
    <li>
        8 / (7 - 5) = 
        <bx:output >
            #8/(7-5)#
        </bx:output>
    </li>

</ol>